{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310648,"nonce":"ZC3Cr15SS0pEp0hToxtvp1DFPtA=","title":"FIXED — `for (v in map)` iterated KEYS not values (silent wrong value + SIGSEGV on String keys). Pre-existing, NOT a monomorphization bug.","message":"**FIXED 2026-06-22 (commit \"fix(map): for-in over a map iterates VALUES, not keys\").** `for (v in map)` in Haxe iterates the map's VALUES (`for (k in map.keys())` gives keys). Two stacked bugs made single-variable map for-in bind the KEY:\n1. **hir_to_mir** (`lower_for_in`, ~29850): single-var map for-in lowered to `haxe_{int,string,object}map_keys_to_array` + indexed access → bound the loop var to each KEY. `for (v in {1=\u003e10,2=\u003e20}) sum+=v` gave **3** (1+2) not 30.\n2. **ast_lowering** (~11600): typed the loop variable as `key_type_id`. For `Map\u003cString,Int\u003e` that typed `v` as String, so `sum+=v` (sum:Int) compiled as **string concat** and cast the Int value to a string pointer → **SIGSEGV**.\n\nFIX: iterate `values_to_array` directly for single-var (mirrors the keys path), and type the loop var as `value_type_id`. k=\u003ev unchanged (keys_to_array + per-key `map.get`). NOTE: tried keys-array + wildcard-key `get()` first — the unbound String key temporary got DROPPED before the lookup → SIGSEGV; the values-array approach avoids it. Verified all Int/String key×value combos, k=\u003ev intact, `for(k in m.keys())` still keys. Test: compiler/tests/haxe/test_map_value_iteration.hx.\n\n**IMPORTANT — causation:** this was PRE-EXISTING (R=3 confirmed on pre-session baseline dc73ae25), NOT caused by the cross-module monomorphization work ([[bugs_generic_monomorph_untyped_ctor]]). The `for(v in map)` path is special-cased in hir_to_mir BEFORE method-call lowering, so the mono changes never touched it. Found via RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR (saw `keys_to_array` + `cast i32 to string`), per darmie's \"check the MIR dump\" steer. A/B time-travel to confirm pre-existence was the wrong instinct — the MIR dump localized it directly.\n\nSEPARATE still-open: `for(k in m.keys())` and `m.iterator()` EXPLICIT calls panic 101 (unresolvable extern Import cross-module) — same residual class as List.iterator in [[bugs_generic_monomorph_untyped_ctor]], pre-existing, not this bug.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_map_for_in_iterates_keys` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}